      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "After establishing a model of ischemia, perfusion in the ischemic area was considerably disturbed. Examination by means of 133xenon-clearance after intramyocardiac injection showed strongly delayed flowing-off compared with controls. Counterpulsation accelerates the flowing-off (perfusion). Untreated control animals reveal after inducing the model ischemia a crucial decrease of ATP concentration and an excessive increase of lactate concentration in the ischemic area. Counterpulsation may inhibit further decrease of ATP in the ischemic area."},
